function rules(){showModal('Game rules',`<p class="rules-copy">The dice chart is unchanged. Three outs ends a half-inning. Choose 3, 6, or 9 innings; ties go to extras.</p><table class="rules-grid">${Object.entries(RULES).map(([k,v])=>`<tr><td>${k}</td><td>${v[1]}</td></tr>`).join('')}</table><div class="rules-copy"><p>Hits move every runner the number of bases hit. Walks move forced runners. Ordinary outs hold runners. Double plays retire the batter plus the runner nearest home (one out if empty or already two out). Sacrifice flies advance every runner one base unless they make the third out.</p><p><strong>Bunt:</strong> each team gets one bunt per three scheduled innings: 1 in a 3-inning game, 2 in 6, or 3 in 9. Tap Bunt and confirm to roll. An even dice total is a bunt single; an odd total retires the batter. Both results advance existing runners exactly one base, except when the batter makes the third out. No run scores on that third out. Bunt singles count as hits; sacrifice bunt outs with runners aboard and fewer than two outs count as SH rather than AB.</p><p><strong>Clutch Batter:</strong> each team gets one Clutch Batter per three scheduled innings: 1 in a 3-inning game, 2 in 6, or 3 in 9. Uses are available from the start. Each at-bat can be rerolled once. Use it after seeing a result, before your next roll or confirming the half-inning. Both dice reroll using the same batting approach; the new result is final, even if worse. The original play is completely reversed, including runs, outs, and stats. You may use it on a third out or provisional game-ending roll.</p><p><strong>A little skill:</strong> save your clutch for a high-leverage situation. The Odds panel compares swinging and bunting for the current base situation. Your decision is when to spend your bunt and reroll; player cards retain equal odds.</p><p>At three outs, tap <strong>Keep play & end inning</strong> when you’re happy with the result. This leaves room to use Clutch Batter. Online opponents receive each individual roll immediately after it saves; they do not need to wait for the inning to finish.</p><p>Four-card rule: a player already on base is skipped in the batting order. No steals, extra-base choices, or push notifications.</p><p>Leagues have 3–12 teams, equal regular-season games per team, then a single-elimination playoff. With an odd number of teams, games per team must be even. Standings use win percentage, wins, head-to-head, run differential, then runs scored.</p></div>`);}
async function lobby(){const g=enter('lobby');session=null;current=null;renderLobby('Connecting…');try{await restoreAccount();if(g!==generation)return;accountLabel();if(!Cloud.user){renderLobby();return;}await Cloud.closeWaitingGames();if(g!==generation)return;keep(g,await Cloud.watchList(list=>{if(g!==generation)return;onlineList=list;renderLobby();},e=>lobbyError(g,e)));keep(g,await Cloud.watchOpenGames(list=>{if(g!==generation)return;openGames=list;renderLobby();},e=>lobbyError(g,e)));keep(g,await Cloud.watchLeagues(list=>{if(g!==generation)return;leagueList=list;renderLobby();},e=>lobbyError(g,e)));}catch(e){lobbyError(g,e);}}
